Thanks both — you're right.

@bbrowning: the `split(..., 1)` version stopped the crash but silently dropped the 2nd+ tool call, which is worse. I've reworked `extract_tool_calls` to split on all `<|action_start|><|plugin|>` markers and return a `ToolCall` per block, with leading text preserved as content; single-call / empty-args / plain-text / malformed inputs are unchanged. Repro: `...<|action_start|><|plugin|>{"name":"get_weather",...}<|action_end|><|action_start|><|plugin|>{"name":"get_time",...}<|action_end|>` → old: ValueError; new: two tool calls. Being honest on the real-world question: the official InternLM2 template emits one tool call per turn, so multi-marker output isn't part of the normal protocol — it shows up when the model misbehaves (InternLM2 tool output is known to be unstable), so this is a robustness fix, but silently dropping data is worse than the crash.

@hclsys: added a streaming-path test feeding the two markers in separate deltas.

Two honest notes: (1) the branch is well behind `main` now and will need a rebase — happy to do that. (2) #48348 is touching this same parser for the adjacent 'whole tool call in one delta' streaming case; if you'd prefer these consolidated or think #48348 supersedes this, just say and I'll rebase accordingly or close.

